AmiStudio Host - changes

0.1.10 (2026-10-19) - fix: the Host crashed at "Sign in..." on Fedora 44 / Nobara
- Crash fix (Rich, Nobara, AmiDrive 0.1.2 "Sign in..." -> "Service Crash: amistudio-hostd"): the static release
  binary resolved accounts.google.com for the 0.1.9 sign-in check with glibc's getaddrinfo, which in a static
  program dlopen()s the system's NSS modules (Fedora: hosts: files myhostname resolve [!UNAVAIL=return] dns).
  libnss_myhostname.so.2 pulled in Fedora 44's own libc.so.6 (newer glibc than the Host was linked with), which died
  with SIGFPE (divide by zero) in __libc_early_init and took the whole Host down, for every sign-in method (0, 1, 2).
  Host 0.1.8 never looked up a name itself (rclone and Chromium resolve their own), so it was not affected.
  Now names are looked up by the system's `getent ahosts` in a child process (the system's NSS with the system's
  libc), numeric addresses with inet_pton, localhost directly (src/plat_posix.c plat_resolve; client/ashc.c inside
  the Host uses the same). The static build wraps glibc's NSS calls (getaddrinfo, gethostbyname*, getnameinfo,
  getservby*, getpw*, getgr*; also the ones OpenSSL references) to src/nss_off.c with -Wl,--wrap, so no NSS code is
  linked at all. No getent on a system: names cannot be resolved (logged as "cannot connect"), the Host stays up.
- The sign-in check now gives up after 8 s (connect and read) instead of 15 + 30 s, then the sign-in goes on.
- Tests: the static binary (and the tarball's) contains no NSS symbols or NSS loader strings; under bwrap with an
  nsswitch.conf whose test NSS module crashes when loaded into amistudio-hostd (and resolves the check's host name
  in getent), AUTH_START 2 reaches the fake Google by name and the Host stays up (test build and static binary);
  sign-in check answers: chunked 400 refusal, odd bytes, empty, endless redirects, no answer (8 s) - no crash, only a
  real "Error 4xx: code" page refuses. Also checked by hand: the shipped 0.1.9 vs this build in a Fedora 44 container
  rootfs (its own nsswitch.conf and glibc): 0.1.9 exits with SIGFPE on AUTH_START 0/1/2, this build answers; and
  under -fsanitize=address,undefined (no reports).

0.1.9 (2026-10-19) - Google sign-in in AmiSurf, sign-in check, AmiSurf 0.87 engine
- Bundled browser engine: AmiSurf 0.87's asb-chromed (hardcopi/amistudio-browser 6493b84, was 0.85 e762b82), with
  the Host's 7 engine patches rebased (conflicts only in asbc.h's message enum and host.c's client-connect line, both
  sides kept). New in the engine: ASBC_BMARKS (45) - the bookmark list (`url<TAB>title<TAB>folder` lines) after the
  client's `bookmarks` command and whenever it changes, for AmiSurf 0.87's bookmarks bar and Bookmarks menu; an
  optional 4th folder column in bookmarks.tsv (Folder field on the internal Bookmarks page; older engines keep it);
  the internal pages server closes idle (preconnected) sockets without replying (a 403 on one was shown as the next
  page). Chromium unchanged (ungoogled-chromium 155.0.8059.79-1). tools/fetch-engine.sh, engine-patches/, docs.
- amidrive AUTH_START 2: the sign-in URL for the Host's own browser engine, so AmiDrive can open it in AmiSurf on the
  Amiga (the engine runs on this PC, so Google's redirect to 127.0.0.1:53682 reaches rclone). Without a browser engine
  method 2 is still URL-only (the URL works in any browser on this PC); Hosts up to 0.1.8 treat 2 as 0.
  `amistudio-hostd amidrive signin --amisurf`.
- AUTH 0 gains a trailing flags byte (1 = this Host has a browser engine, 2 = the desktop browser of a method-0
  sign-in could not open); clients that ignore it are unaffected. Sessions joining a sign-in with AUTH_START 1/2 get
  the URL (also for a running desktop sign-in), never AUTH 1. Refusal texts shortened to ~140 bytes; the AUTH 2/3
  text always equals the RESULT message.
- Sign-in check: before rclone starts the Host asks Google whether it accepts the AmiStudio OAuth client with
  rclone's redirect. Google refusing it (the shipped 0.1.8 client answers "Error 400: redirect_uri_mismatch") now
  ends the sign-in at once with that reason instead of a browser on Google's error page. `amidrive_auth_check no`
  turns it off. The request carries the public client ID only.
- Tests: the check against a local HTTPS stand-in for Google (refusal, pass, off), AUTH_START 2 with and without a
  browser engine, flags byte, joiners (URL vs step), refusal length = RESULT text, cancel, no secret in argv or logs.

0.1.8 (2026-10-19) - Google Drive (amidrive)
- New built-in service `amidrive` v1 (src/svc_amidrive.c; docs/PROTOCOL.md "amidrive v1", docs/SERVICES.md
  "Google Drive"): mounts Google Drive with the bundled rclone 1.75.2 through FUSE at `amidrive_mountpoint` (the
  launcher: `<AmiStudio drawer>/Google Drive`), for AmiDrive and the launcher. Sign-in in the PC's desktop browser
  (`rclone authorize drive` with the real desktop environment), status/flush/unmount through rclone's rc, open-file
  refusal with a path list, pending uploads kept in `{state}/amidrive/cache/`, `Drive.mount` marker
  (tab-separated, path last), drawer icon parked/placed, `--drive-use-trash` always on, non-empty mount point
  refused, copied/moved drawer detected (`drawer.path`; a copy's cache is set aside), `invalid_grant` -> sign-in
  expired, leftover rclone/stale mount cleared at start, rclone crash -> lazy unmount + one retry, one
  mount/unmount/flush/sign-out at a time (others get busy), `amidrive.lock` so two Hosts never share one Drive.
  Lifecycle (Rich, 19.10.2026): mounted only when AmiStudio/AmiDrive start (CONNECT flag 1), flushed and unmounted
  when the Host stops; `amidrive_keeps_host` (default no).
- CONNECT right after the last file of a lazily unmounted Drive was closed waits up to 3 s for that rclone to end
  (was: busy at once while it was still exiting).
- CLI: `amistudio-hostd amidrive status|signin|connect|flush|unmount [--force|--later]|signout`, also in ash-cli.
- Services may have `busy()` (keeps the Host up without a client; CONFDIR/busy for the launcher's watcher) and
  `init()` hooks; all services now stop in parallel on shutdown.
- host-defaults.conf next to the binary (read before host.conf): the release tarball's AmiStudio OAuth client. The
  client secret is filled in from AMIDRIVE_CLIENT_SECRET by dist/mktarball.sh only (empty if unset).
- http.c: http_req (any method, headers, body) for the token revoke and the account lookup.
- config: `#` inside "double quotes" is no longer a comment; quoted values are unquoted.
- Release tarball: engine/rclone/rclone, LICENSES/rclone-COPYING.txt + RCLONE-VERSION.txt (tools/fetch-rclone.sh,
  sha256-pinned), services/amidrive/Google Drive.info (from the AmiDrive release), host-defaults.conf (0600).
  The Host is GPL v3 (LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt; mktarball.sh no longer says "licence not chosen").
- Docs: INSTALL.md (fuse3, desktop-browser sign-in, files), PROTOCOL.md, SERVICES.md.
- Tests: test/amidrive_tests.py (80 checks with an rclone alias remote of a local folder: space in the path, kill
  and restart, pending uploads, open files, non-empty mount point, copied/moved drawer, stop-on-quit, keeps_host,
  sign-in URL/cancel without the secret on argv or in logs, expired token, self-contained scan).

Also in 0.1.8 (docs and tests since 0.1.7):
- Documented the self-contained install the AmiStudio launcher (0.1.8+) uses on AmiKit: everything under its
  AmiStudio/Host drawer via --confdir, data_dir/--data-dir, ASB_DOWNLOADS, HOME, XDG_* and TMPDIR (docs/INSTALL.md
  "Self-contained install"; run-host.sh header). The standalone Linux install (~/.config, ~/.local/share, systemd
  user unit) is unchanged; its Files table now also lists what Chromium, fontconfig, PulseAudio and NSS keep.
- Test: app_tests selfcontained_tests (both bundled services with everything under one folder: profiles, Host id,
  downloads and Chromium's HOME/TMPDIR files inside it, nothing Chromium-like new in the real ~ or /tmp).
- Tests no longer leave PulseAudio daemons behind (one per throw-away HOME used to stay running after every
  ASH_TEST_BROWSER=1 run): test/pulse_guard.py passes the user's own PULSE_SERVER/PULSE_COOKIE to the test engines
  (as the launcher's run-host.sh does), turns libpulse autospawn off, and at the end (and at exit) stops any
  pulseaudio whose HOME is under that run's test folder, nothing else. New checks: no daemon started under the test
  HOME, none left behind. The self-contained test counts the user's own daemon updating ~/.config/pulse as allowed.

0.1.7 (2026-10-18) - bundled engine on AmiSurf 0.85
- Bundled engine moved from AmiSurf 0.83 (bd10794) to AmiSurf 0.85 (e762b82 on AmiSurf main, the published
  0.85 engine). AmiSurf (browser service): download status from a browser-wide CDP connection
  ("Downloading NAME to FOLDER", "Downloaded NAME (N KB) to FOLDER", failed/canceled), tabs the page opens
  (target=_blank, window.open, context menu) shown at once and sent as TABS, window.open popups no longer blank, a
  popup that closes itself falls back to its opener, a fresh frame when switching to a background tab.
- That browser-wide connection is off in app mode (AmiDiscord): app popups are still caught and closed, app
  downloads keep their names and DOWNLOAD messages.
- Engine patches 0001-0007 rebased onto e762b82 (same changes; 0002 also keeps AmiSurf's browser connection off in
  app mode). Tests: app_tests tabs_tests (browser mode: new tab, popup, popup closing, tab switch frame, download
  status + file, one event per download), app mode checks that the connection stays off; bundle tests take the
  folder name from the tarball.

0.1.6 (2026-10-18) - AmiDiscord view findings against 0.1.4; quit-when-unused for the launcher
- RESIZE restarts the screencast at the new size: frames are the new view size at once (they came scaled down to
  the old size, e.g. 571x400 for 1000x700, until FMT was re-sent). Re-sending FMT still works.
- Zoom: frames are always exactly the view size with the content magnified (zoom-in gave unzoomed CSS-size frames,
  500x350 at 200 % in a 1000x700 view) and the engine's "frame != view, re-applying viewport" log loop is gone.
  Under zoom the frames are full-size screenshots (one in flight); zoom rounding (+-3 px) is fitted exactly.
- App mode: a new client starts at the default zoom with no find state; the same client reconnecting or taking
  its slot over keeps them. The Host tells asbc2 backends who the client is (first frame: CMD "asbhost client
  KEY", same identity as the session-slot rule); older engines ignore it.
- New built-in service `control` v1 (paired or loopback, like fetch): QUIT_WHEN_UNUSED [u16 grace s, default 10],
  QUIT_CANCEL, QUIT_STATUS -> QUIT_STATE u8 state u16 others u16 grace. No other client -> the Host stops at once
  (engines close Chromium cleanly, exit 0); else it stops grace seconds after the last client, also with exit_idle
  off; a reconnect within the grace keeps it up. hostinfo lists `service control 1 up`; older Hosts answer status 2.
  `allow_quit no` / `--no-remote-quit` turns it off (always-on Hosts).
- Engine patch 0007 (patches 0001-0006 unchanged). docs/PROTOCOL.md "control v1" and "View size, zoom and
  per-client state (0.1.6)". New tests: app_tests view_tests (app + browser mode), control tests in run_tests.py.

0.1.5 (2026-10-18) - fixes from AmiDiscord's tests against 0.1.4
- FILEPUT cancel needs only u32 req + u8 flags=2 (5 bytes); the full 11-byte form stays valid. A truncated
  non-cancel FILEPUT header ends the request with FILEDONE 2 instead of being dropped silently.
- UNREAD: no unread state (count, dot or favicon badge) on logged-out pages (`/`, `/login`, `/register`, `/reset`,
  `/verify`; `ASB_APP_NOUNREAD`): Discord's login page favicon swap was reported as a badge. The plain favicon is
  learned again after login (also for Discord's in-page /login -> /channels navigation).
- APPINFO gets a u32 max upload in bytes after the caps (ASB_APP_MAXUPLOAD, clamped 1..4095 MB). Appended, so
  0.1.4-era clients still parse it; clients must ignore trailing bytes.
- OPENURL url at most 1023 bytes (fits AmiDiscord's 1024-byte buffer); a longer URL is never cut, the client gets
  a STATUS "Link too long to open outside the app" instead.
- One data/download folder rule: `<app data>` = ASB_STATE, else `<data>/<app id>`, `<data>` = the Host's {state}
  (--data-dir / data_dir, default ~/.local/share/amistudio-host), now passed to services as AMISTUDIO_HOST_DATA;
  downloads in `<app data>/downloads` (ASB_DOWNLOADS overrides). Bundled amidiscord: `<data>/amidiscord/downloads`.
  A service block without ASB_STATE (and AmiSurf's `browser` data) now follows --data-dir too. asb-chromed in app
  mode without engine.sh no longer defaults to AmiKit's Downloads drawer.
- Engine patch 0006 (patches 0001-0005 unchanged). docs/PROTOCOL.md "Details (0.1.5)". New tests in
  test/app_tests.py (M3 logged-out unread, M4 short cancel/APPINFO/OPENURL limit, dlpath_tests).

0.1.4 (2026-10-17) - AmiDiscord app mode
- M0: a dropped client no longer locks a `max_clients` service: when the same client reconnects (same paired token,
  or same client id from the same address on loopback) the Host closes its stale session and the new one gets OK
  instead of status 5 (busy). Other clients still get busy. Also on the compat port. plat_shutdown() added (POSIX +
  Windows). 7 new tests.
- M0: the ASBC FRAME header is documented in docs/PROTOCOL.md, including the pixel-format byte (offset 13) of fmt 3
  tiles; the same fix to AmiSurf's asbc.h comment is engine patch 0001.
- M1: app mode for a new `amidiscord` service (AmiDiscord, replacing Matrix Chat): the bundled engine is mounted a
  second time in app mode (env ASB_APP=amidiscord, discord.com/app, max_clients 1, log amidiscord.log); Chrome
  stays up 30 min after the last AmiDiscord client (`amidiscord_idle`, --amidiscord-idle, 0 = never),
  `bundled_amidiscord no` / --no-bundled-amidiscord turns it off. Engine patch 0002 (chrome/appmode.inc, all gated
  on ASB_APP): start URL, host allowlist, external links/new windows cancelled in Chrome and sent as OPENURL
  (op 48), allowlisted popups open in the page, fallback title; no tabs, asb:// pages, bookmarks, history,
  suggestions, password manager or save/source/PDF; reduced motion (prefers-reduced-motion + frame throttling,
  `CMD app reducedmotion 0|1`) - test animation 3.8 MB/5 s instead of 115 MB; Chrome muted (`--mute-audio`, no
  audio sink) so only the Amiga's own notifications sound. engine.sh keeps app data in
  ~/.local/share/amistudio-host/<app>. Tests: test/app_tests.py + test/app_page.py (local fake app) and the real
  discord.com/login page (render only, private profile and ports, no login).
- M2: per-service data. New exec placeholders `{state}` (the Host's data folder: ~/.local/share/amistudio-host,
  %LOCALAPPDATA%\AmiStudio-Host, `data_dir` / --data-dir) and `{config}`; the bundled amidiscord service sets both
  ASB_STATE={state}/amidiscord and ASB_CONFIG={state}/amidiscord/config, and engine.sh now honours a given
  ASB_CONFIG. Graceful stop: the Host sends SIGTERM to the backend alone and waits `stop_timeout` (default 15 s,
  amidiscord 20) before ending its process group (Windows unchanged). Engine patch 0003: in app mode asb-chromed
  closes Chrome with Browser.close on SIGTERM and on its idle exit, so the Discord login persists; app-mode
  defaults no longer fall back to AmiSurf's ~/.config/amisurf; `CMD app logout`. 9 new tests (fake login in
  cookie + localStorage survives Host and engine restarts; logout clears it).
- M3: notifications for AmiDiscord. Engine patch 0004 (chrome/appnotify.inc, app mode only): Notification API +
  ServiceWorker showNotification shim on the allowlisted origins (no DOM scraping, no Runtime.enable), permission
  granted up front, unread count/dot from the title pattern table and favicon badge, focus/visibility emulation
  (`CMD app focus F V`; hidden = no frames but notifications continue; no client = unfocused + hidden),
  `CMD app notifyact`. The real discord.com login page gets the shim (checked, not logged in). 23 new tests with a
  local fake page (test/app_page.py /notify).
- M4: the AmiDiscord client protocol, capability-gated (docs/PROTOCOL.md "App mode messages"; engine patch 0005,
  chrome/appproto.inc): client -> Host CAPS 22, FOCUS 23, NOTIFYACT 24, FILEPUT 25; Host -> client NOTIFY 45,
  NOTIFYCLOSE 46, UNREAD 47 (on change, max 2/s, latest one after CAPS/reconnect), OPENURL 48 (now only with its
  cap; else STATUS), FILEREQ 49, FILEDONE 50 (uploads via the page's file chooser, 25 MB limit), DOWNLOAD 51
  (exact Host path), APPINFO 52 (reply to CAPS, host caps 63). clipboard.writeText -> CLIP. Without CAPS, and
  always in AmiSurf's `browser` service, nothing changes. 23 new tests.
- Engine patches: the Host's changes to AmiSurf's asb-chromed live in engine-patches/ (git format-patch mails
  against the pinned AmiSurf commit, for AmiSurf to `git am`); tools/fetch-engine.sh applies them, and
  tools/engine-work.sh init|export|build is the work tree for editing them. AmiSurf's repo is not touched.

0.1.3 (2026-10-17)
- `amistudio-hostd status` no longer hangs when another program holds the port: 2 s connect/read timeout
  (ASH_TIMEOUT_MS overrides) and a clear message - "nothing listening", "in use by a program that is not an
  AmiStudio Host (no ASH answer within 2.0 s / it answered something else)". ashc_set_timeout() in the C client
  (not on Amiga builds); `ash-cli info` uses 5 s. Reported by AmiSurf.
- Host idle shutdown (`--exit-idle MIN`, host.conf `exit_idle`, run-host.sh `--host-idle` / `--idle`): the Host
  stops after MIN minutes in which NO client connection was open and none was opened. Every ASH connection counts
  (AmiSurf sessions, the launcher's hostinfo checks, pair, fetch) and so does the 9223 compat port; discovery
  broadcasts do not. The engine idles on its own (`browser_idle`). Off by default (systemd). Reported by AmiSurf.
- run-host.sh: `--idle MIN` now sets both the engine idle and the Host idle shutdown (the AmiKit behaviour);
  `--engine-idle MIN` and `--host-idle MIN` set one each.
- Browser data layout confirmed identical to AmiSurf's AmiKit Host/data: config/ and profile/ (and WidevineCdm/)
  copy straight into ~/.local/share/amistudio-host/browser; tested.
- Engine pin unchanged (bd10794; asb-chromed source identical since 4bb4f04).

0.1.2 (2026-10-17)
- The release tarball bundles AmiSurf's browser engine, so one Host install serves AmiSurf with no extra download:
  engine/asb-chromed (static, built from AmiSurf 0.83 wip/083 bd10794) and engine/chromium/ (ungoogled-chromium
  portablelinux 155.0.8059.79-1 x86_64, headless, unmodified; chromedriver removed) - the same engine AmiSurf 0.83's
  AmiKit edition ships. Built with tools/fetch-engine.sh (pinned commit, Chromium sha256 checked); `make tarball`.
- The bundled engine is mounted as the "browser" service automatically (ASBC v2 handshake, proto 2) when
  INSTALLDIR/engine/engine.sh exists and host.conf has no browser service. host.conf `bundled_browser no` or
  --no-bundled-browser turns it off; `browser_idle MIN` / --browser-idle MIN (default 30) stops an unused engine,
  which the Host restarts on demand.
- Browser data lives outside the install folder: ~/.local/share/amistudio-host/browser (config/ = bookmarks,
  history, settings, passwords; profile/ = Chromium profile; ASB_STATE overrides). Engine log: CONFDIR/browser.log.
- run-host.sh: --port, --idle MIN, --lan, --pair (print a pairing code), --background (detach; safe to run twice),
  other options go to amistudio-hostd. Restores lost exec bits.
- install-user.sh installs the whole folder to ~/.local/lib/amistudio-host (swapped in on update) and links
  ~/.local/bin/amistudio-hostd to it, so the systemd user unit runs the bundled engine. Settings and data are kept.
- New exec placeholder {port2}: a second free loopback port (the engine's private Chrome debug port).
- LICENSES/: Chromium licence + credits, ungoogled-chromium and portablelinux licences, AmiSurf's attributions,
  stb_image / QOI / OpenSSL / zlib / zstd notices, ENGINE-VERSION.txt.
- Tests: 97 with ASH_TEST_BROWSER=1 and the tarball built (22 end-to-end on the unpacked tarball: page render,
  data outside the install dir, reaper + restart, --pair, --background --lan, install-user.sh + systemd unit).

0.1.1 (2026-10-17)
- Backend reaper: a thread checks every child-process service (asb-chromed and co.) once a second, so a backend
  that exits is reaped at once instead of staying a zombie until the next client connects. The exit (status or
  signal) is logged, hostinfo shows "idle exited signal N" / "idle exited status N", and the next client starts
  it again. "start boot" backends are restarted by the reaper itself (5 s back-off after a quick crash).
  Reported by AmiSurf.
- Re-pairing replaces the old token: a pair request from the same Amiga (same client id, or the same name from
  the same address when no id is sent) drops that Amiga's previous token instead of adding a second entry. The
  log names the replaced id. PAIR_REQ takes an optional third line, a stable client id. Reported by AmiSurf.
- `amistudio-hostd tokens` shows when each token was last used (and the client id, if any). The tokens file
  gains optional u=LAST_USED and c=CLIENT_ID fields (written at most once a minute per token); 0.1 files still
  load. `revoke` unchanged.
- The Host's own update check reads the "component host" block of the AmiStudio-Releases manifest (PC parts are
  component blocks, which Amiga launchers skip); an "app host" block is still understood.
- New platform call plat_proc_reap() (POSIX + Windows) returns how a backend exited.
- Tests: 80 with ASH_TEST_BROWSER=1 (75 without), incl. the update check against a local manifest, reaper on a fake backend and on real asb-chromed,
  boot-restart, re-pair by name and by client id, 0.1 tokens-file compatibility.

0.1 (2026-10-17)
- First version: ASH v1 on 9220, pairing + tokens + bans, LAN discovery, hostinfo, fetch proxy, child-process
  service plugin (asb-chromed mounted unchanged, ASBC compat port), Windows layer (compile-checked), systemd unit.
